executor edits the ORIGINAL opaque product photograph into a COMPLETE scene, with visual fidelity review; there is no extraction, alpha mask or pixel-lock guarantee. Otherwise the product is LOCKED_PRODUCT_ASSET and local code composites its exact pixels. Use SCENE_DISPLAY_REFERENCES for environment, photographic quality and plausible installation only; never copy their products, text or watermark. Choose a credible European or North American use setting from THIS product's purpose, not a generic empty showroom. Decide location, mounting/support plane, believable scale, lens/view distance, source-compatible angle, directional light, contact shadow and coherent depth. Surrounding architecture, garden or restrained props may establish context OUTSIDE the product area; no prop may intersect its outline or appear through retained material. Give each requested direction meaningfully different setting/composition, not merely a wall recolour. For SCENE assess physical scale against doors, benches, siding, bricks or mounting posts. Use confirmed product dimensions when supplied. Otherwise provide a clearly labelled suggested size/range and rationale in scene_scale_advice (concise Chinese); separate confirmed dimensions from recommendations, never present a visual estimate as measured fact. State mounting/placement height and plausible fixing approach as recommendations, not unseen hardware facts. Put the relative product-to-setting size and clearances into scene_execution.composition and placement_plane, and execute corresponding width_fraction/center coordinates. Keep recommendations out of the rendered image. Populate scene_execution with your actual placement, camera, light and atmosphere. If scene_direct_reference_edit is true, execution_prompt must request the complete scene containing the same product from the original photo: preserve visible contour, holes, parts, orientation, proportions and material while integrating real light and mounting. Do not plan segmentation or mask repairs. Otherwise art-direct an EMPTY background and execution_prompt must request ONLY this empty background: no product, animal, silhouette, sign, hand or lettering. Choose the placement plane and position to fit the composition; reserve that exact area. A source photo permits scale/translation/in-plane rotation only: choose a compatible camera, never invent unseen product surfaces. scene_execution uses normalized center_x/center_y/width_fraction and shadow_dx/shadow_dy/blur as fractions of canvas; shadow points away from the planned light. Do not substitute a generic wall/center/shadow preset. Also specify camera_angle, view_distance, light_direction, light_height, light_softness, environment_brightness and contact_shadow. The background generator reads these, and the compositor executes your numeric position, scale, rotation, shadow offsets, blur and opacity; they must agree with those photographic decisions. ")
